I'm working on a Twincat project where I need to use 1 PLC to manage a set of stepper controllers driven by simple digital outputs.




I've got a function block for driving the stepper when commanded that works in prototypes and I'd like to apply here. Basics of Function Block:




FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_StepperDriver
VAR_INPUT
    bEnable : BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
    bDirOut : BOOL;
    bPulseOut : BOOL;
    bInhibitOut : BOOL;
END_VAR


//Turn the bPulseOut variable to true and false every cycle





My initial architecture involved organizing each controller's input and outputs into a structure, with an array of this structure representing the collection, like so:




VAR_GLOBAL
    Controllers : ARRAY[0..7] OF ST_Stepper;

END_VAR


TYPE ST_STEPPER
STRUCT
    bLimitSwitch1Engaged AT %I* : BOOL;
    bLimitSwitch2Engaged AT %I* : BOOL;
    bInhibit AT %Q* : BOOL; //Output that turns on controller
