    bPulse AT %Q* : BOOL; //Rising Edge of true pushes motor 1 step
    fbStepperDriver : FB_StepperDriver;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE





Where I get stuck is trying to assign the output variables of the function block to the related variables of the structure (e.g. bDir being assigned to the FB's bDirOut). Is there a way to do this within the structure, or will I have to do this in a POU on startup? Attempting to use the standard 

=>

 operator doesn't seem to be working.

For your particular question, the answer is:




PROGRAM MAIN
VAR
    controllers : ARRAY[0..7] OF ST_STEPPER;
    index   : INT;
END_VAR

FOR index := 0 TO 7 BY 1 DO
    controllers[index].fbStepperDriver(
        bEnable := TRUE,
        bDirOut => controllers[index].bDir,
